# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
# `dist/` itself must EXIST on a fresh checkout even when empty: `crates/designer`'s
# `#[derive(RustEmbed)] #[folder = ".../designer/dist"]` is a compile-time error when the
# folder is absent, so `cargo build --workspace` — and therefore `just ci` — fails on any
# machine that has not run the SPA build. That is what kept GitHub CI red from 2026-08-24
# while `just ci` passed locally, where the directory happened to exist. An EMPTY dist is
# already a supported state (see `just ci`'s npm check and `crates/designer/src/assets.rs`):
# the server builds and serves no UI. So ignore the contents, keep the directory.
dist/*
!dist/.gitkeep
dist-ssr
*.local

# eieio-m9s.11: written by `just shapes` (which runs the `response_shapes` test in
# `crates/cli` and `crates/designer`), read by `src/lib/api/schema-parity.test.ts` and
# `src/lib/api/mock-parity.test.ts`. An artifact, not a maintained list — see those Rust tests'
# module docs for why it must be regenerated rather than trusted.
#
# Still not committed, deliberately (eieio-m9s.42 re-weighed it). A committed copy would be a
# second source of truth for the daemon's own schemas, and one that goes stale silently: the
# parity check would then compare `types.ts` against a snapshot of the schemas rather than the
# schemas, which is the drift it exists to catch, wearing the check's own clothes. A fresh
# clone pays one `just shapes` instead — the same trade `dist/` and `crates/expr-wasm/pkg`
# already make, and it is a prerequisite of `just test-designer` for exactly that reason.
src/lib/api/__generated__/

